<title>INDIA: Indian soybean up, oil, meal steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean up, oil, meal steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were up in plant delivery on better demand on Tuesday, dealers said. Prices were up by 100 rupees per tonne in plant delivery condition but market prices were steady.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were steady in limited trading activity. The undertone was steady.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were steady but rapeseed extraction prices were down on lack of demand. Soymeal yellow was $276-278 for new season's November, December and January shipment.</p>
<p>For current season soymeal yellow was $292-293 per tonne September-October shipment. Rapeseed extraction was $126 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,400 rupees FOR Bedibunder and was 4,350 rupees FOR Bhavnagar port.</p>
